  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "J.Thavamani Kumar vs The Food Safety Officer on 11 December, 2024 Author: N.Anand Venkatesh Bench: N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.(MD)No. Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 11.12.2024 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.(MD) No.18261 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.(MD) No.12187 of 2022 J.Thavamani Kumar ... Pet Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Alanganallur Union Registration No.108, Food Safety and Drug Administration, Office of the Designated Officer, Health and Family Welfare Training Centre Campus, Vishwanathapuram 625 503, Madurai District. ... Re PRAYER : Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 4 Criminal Procedure Code, to call for the entire records pertaining case in STC.No.13 of 2022 pending on the file of the learned Judici Magistrate Vadipatti Madurai District and quash the same as against petitioner. For Petitioner : Mr.R.Anand For Respondent : Mr.A.Albert James Government Advocate (Crl. Si 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No J.Thavamani Kumar vs The Food Safety Officer on 11 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/74402654/ 1 ORDER",
    "facts": "2.The respondent has filed a private complaint against the petitioner for offence under Sections 51, 58 and 59(i) of the 'Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006' (hereinafter referred to as 'the Act' for brevity).",
    "arguments": "4.Apart from other grounds that were raised by the learned counsel for the petitioner, the main ground that was raised was that the petitioner was denied an opportunity of sending the sample for further test as provided under Section 46(4) of the Act."
  },
